        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      body {\n        background-color: #ffeeaa;\n        color: #076b03;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h2>The Tradition of Music</h2>\n    <p>Music is one of the oldest forms of human expression. Across every culture and era, people have used music to tell stories, mark celebrations, process grief, and build community.</p>\n    <p>From drumming circles to concert halls, music takes countless forms — each shaped by the people and places that created it.</p>\n\n    <section>\n      <h2>Punk Rock</h2>\n      <p>Punk rock emerged in the mid-1970s as a raw, fast, and rebellious reaction to mainstream music.</p>\n      <p>Bands like The Clash and the Ramones stripped music down to its essentials — three chords, a loud amp, and something to say.</p>\n      <p>Punk wasn't just a sound. It was a statement about who gets to make music and what music is allowed to be.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <h2>Music Today</h2>\n    <p>Today, music is more accessible than ever. Streaming platforms give listeners instant access to millions of songs from every corner of the world.</p>\n    <p>At the same time, new artists face new challenges — standing out in a crowded landscape, earning a living from their work, and finding an audience that connects with what they're making.</p>\n    <p>But the tradition continues. People are still picking up instruments, writing songs, and sharing what they hear in their heads with the rest of the world.</p>\n\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "active": true,
          "folderId": "0"
